    "description": {
      "chat": "",
      "unidentified": "",
      "value": "<p>Create an invisible visual sensor at any point you can see. While concentrating, you see through it as if present. It moves 30 feet per round when looking mainly ahead and down, or 10 feet per round when thoroughly inspecting walls and ceiling. It can move in any direction and pass through openings at least 1 inch across, but not solid barriers or planar portals.</p><p>Without concentration the eye becomes inert until you resume. The material component is a small amount of bat fur.</p><p><strong>Automation boundary:</strong> Move a proxy sensor and enforce concentration, visibility, and barrier limits manually.</p>"
    },
